  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Mount Stuart</strong> rises to 9,419 feet in Washington. It has roughly 5,354 feet of topographic prominence. The Mount Stuart Trail is a 4.2-mile hike with about 1,807 feet of elevation gain. Nearby peaks include Mount Daniel, Disappointment Peak and Seven Fingered Jack. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL); verify current conditions with the official land manager before you go.</p>\n</div>",
